### Register
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Register with the same email again -> 409
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Register with invalid body -> 400
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "123"
}

### Login (stores the token in the "token" variable)
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.token);
%}

### Login with wrong password -> 401
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### Protected endpoint without token -> 401
GET {{host}}/anything

### Protected endpoint with token (404 means the token was accepted, there is no such route yet)
GET {{host}}/anything
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
